ns 3.2% a year to shareholders (3.1% in buybacks and 0.1% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.4% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 21,000 employees, each generates about $364K of revenue, in line with the Industrials median, and revenue has grown 15.7% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $58K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.7M (7x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"score":35.9,"head":"Priced 34% above its $63.63 fair value, but that value is low-confidence and the price is inside its $27.05\u2013$140 range.","pros":["FCF margin 15.9%","Revenue grew 9.3%/yr over 5y","Altman Z in the safe zone","Operating margin expanding 1.3%/yr","Returns 3.2% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 34% above fair value of $63.63","ROIC 6.5% vs WACC 9.2%","EV/EBITDA 18.0x vs sector 13.3x"],"flags":[],"vc":{"base":63.63,"base_src":"dcf","bear":27.05,"bull":140.25,"alt_median":10.91,"n_alt":3,"gap":4.8298,"dispersion":0.5953,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (60% dispersion)","DCF is 483% above the other models' median ($10.91)"]},"med":{"pe":23.0957,"ev_ebitda":13.252,"pfcf":22.4428,"pb":2.9148,"roic":0.1003,"gross_margin":0.2856,"fcf_margin":0.0681,"div_yield":0.0147}},"mc_quantiles":[11.44,19.82,27.05,31.94,37.14,41.77,46.25,50.32,54.62,59.82,64.66,69.76,75.31,83.81,90.4,98.25,108.27,121.35,140.25,176.92,252.97],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.757,"discount_rate":0.047,"terminal_growth":0.003,"exit_multiple":0.006,"base_fcf":0.186},"ticker":"IR","date":"2026-11-27"}